parts.required:
2. Calculate the average interest rate a bank should charge if the following is known:
- The target Return on Equity (ROE) is 20%;
- 2% of total assets will be cash and the rest can be assumed as the loan portfolio;
- Expected bad debts on the loan portfolio are 0.5%;
- The overall average cost of capital is estimated at 6.5%;
- Total operating costs of the bank will amount to 3% on total assets;
- The bank targets a leverage ratio of 10%;
- Taxation is at 28%; and
- ROE = return on assets x leverage.

Please note: some marks are rewarded for formulas and clearly setting out what you are doing.  [10]
